  "pli-tv-kd7:12.1.1": "“Whose meditation is going well” renders _phāsuvihārika_. _Vihāra_ is a common Sutta term for a state of meditation, as in _diṭṭhadhammasukhavihāra_, “a happy (meditation) abiding in this very life”, which is a reference to the four absorptions. _Phāsu_ means “comfortable” or “at ease”. Although this may be understood quite broadly, it seems likely that meditation would be the main connotation. ",
